{"archetypes":[{"name":"resume","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"Legacy pause/resume compatibility is central to this diff and can regress silently across sentinel states.","prompt_body":"Investigate whether the new Step 2a.5 and Step 4 compatibility paths preserve old paused-session behavior without re-running work incorrectly. Pay particular attention to sentinel ordering, missing `.completed/finalize`, missing `.completed/step-2a.5`, and whether failures halt before later reads occur. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"routing","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"The change depends on all Step 3b-to-Step 4 routes converging through a new completion boundary.","prompt_body":"Trace every documented and scripted route from Step 3, Step 3b, Gate B bypasses, and cap-reached paths toward Step 4. Look for any path or prose that still allows Step 4 to run without first passing through the Step 3b completion boundary and FINALIZE. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"shell-fences","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The implementation relies on prompt-embedded bash fences with strict fail-fast and captured-exit semantics.","prompt_body":"Review the modified bash snippets and shell harness additions for `set -euo pipefail`, `set +e` capture blocks, quoting, branch scoping, and completion-marker ordering. Focus on whether SIMPLE artifact writes and FINALIZE failure handling are atomic enough to avoid partially completed state. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"harness","focus_area":"code-quality","weight":1,"rationale":"Most changed code is structural test logic whose assertions must be precise without false positives or blind spots.","prompt_body":"Evaluate the new structural and pause/resume harness assertions for overbroad greps, brittle line-scoped matching, missing negative cases, and accidental acceptance of stale routing variants. Check that the tests would fail for the failure modes described in the plan rather than only proving the current text contains expected substrings. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
